        "sortBy": [
          {
            "desc": true,
            "displayName": "Severity"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Battery proven 2026-08-28 — the history before it is not",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The pack is fitted and proven.** An APCRBC115 went into `mjolnir` on 2026-08-28 and `upsTestResultsSummary` moved `4` (aborted) → `1` (donePass) at 22:45 UTC. `upsBatteryVoltage` left its fabricated `480` for a float reading that moves across `540`–`549` — the step 5 comparison a card cannot fake. Runtime is *not* that comparison: it has sat on exactly `63`, the fabricated value, for 744 of 764 samples since the fit. Charge still reads exactly `100`, which is what a pack at float voltage looks like.\n\n**Anything on these panels before 2026-08-28 is fabricated.** With an empty bay the card invented a flat 100%, 63 minutes and 48.0 V. The trend panels below cross that boundary — widen the time range with that in mind.\n\n**The card tests itself every fortnight, and nothing here watches that.** Read off the NMC on 2026-09-03: `upsAdvTestDiagnosticSchedule` `8` (biweeklySinceLastTest), last test `08/28/2026`. Those are PowerNet OIDs and this module walks the standard UPS-MIB only, so if the card reverted to `never`, `upsTestResultsSummary` would hold `1` forever and no panel here would move. `UpsBatteryUnproven` cannot catch it either — it matches `6` (noTestsInitiated). Check by hand with `scripts/snmp-walk.sh --device mjolnir 1.3.6.1.4.1.318.1.1.1.7.2`; step 6 of `docs/runbooks/fit-the-ups-battery.md`."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Power source",
